        "notes": "# Chromium 155, pinned folders, and Juno that tries every lead\n\n## What's new\n\n- Chromium 155: the browser moves to the newest version, with every security fix Google shipped since 0.1.3, several of them critical. The browser starts again for everyone: 0.1.3's Chromium 154 was now too far behind.\n- Pin folders: a folder's menu has Pin to the top. A pinned folder sits in Pinned with its chats under it.\n- Pinned chats stay pinned: moving a pinned chat into a folder keeps it in Pinned.\n- Git works the way your terminal does: fetch, pull, push and clone run with the git sign-in you already have, after one card. Status, diff and log just run.\n- Commands are always at hand: Juno can run a command whenever a task needs one, without looking for it first.\n\n## Juno finishes more\n\n- Juno opens what it found before saying something is not there: the links in an email it read, the emails a search listed, an attachment, the next page of results.\n- Asking you is for what only you know: Juno no longer hands a task back while it still has a way to do it itself.\n- A draft for an app without its own draft card, like Discord, is no longer just a card in the chat: Juno writes it where it goes and leaves it unsent.\n- Meeting notes keep what was said: a reply that starts with \"no\" no longer drops the promise after it, and notes made by an older version are written again once.\n\n## Fixes\n\n- Searching and filtering on shopping and rental sites no longer asks for a yes. Placing an order still does.\n- Going to the checkout page is no longer a card; paying always is.\n- A run that needed your sign-in no longer ends on a card with only Stop.\n- Faster starts: the page in front is read alongside everything else.",
